WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.380
The red pill has been extended to us once
again, and it could mark the beginning of

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.500
something major.

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:10.840
In summer 2019, Warner Bros. announced that
a new Matrix movie was in the works, and since

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.639
then, people have been wondering whether the
franchise might ultimately extend beyond the

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:15.960
upcoming fourth installment.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.471
Well, according to a recent article in We
Got This Covered, the as-yet-untitled film

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:23.320
will indeed blossom into a second Matrix trilogy.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.020
The article also revealed that,

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:29.020
"[While] Keanu Reeves and Carrie-Anne Moss
are coming back as Neo and Trinity for the

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.940
new movie, it’s unclear as of yet if [they'll]
return for the next two as well."

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.240
Of course, we should remind you that this
is all just a rumor at this point.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:42.360
Still, the possibility of a new Matrix trilogy
begs the question: Would it be worth revisiting

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.680
the franchise for not just one, but three
more films?

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.180
As has been widely reported, Lilly Wachowski,
who co-created the franchise with her sister

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:52.920
Lana, isn't involved in the upcoming installment.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:58.650
As Decider reported back in August 2019, she
hasn't specifically stated why she's not working

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:02.780
on the fourth Matrix film, but it sounds like
she's not feeling particularly inspired by

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.620
the sci-fi genre at the moment.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:05.860
In fact, she revealed that,

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:09.120
"My agent kept sending me stuff, and a lot
of science fiction.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:09.620
Great.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:11.020
It's good stuff, science fiction.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:13.450
You get to talk a lot about a lot of subjects.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:15.920
There's always fabulous subtext in science
fiction.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:19.860
Since my transition, I'm not really interested
in subtext at this time."

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:25.020
As you probably know, Lilly came out as a
transgender woman in 2016, and her sister

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.380
Lana did the same back in 2012.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:32.240
And although Lilly sounds a bit disenchanted
with the sci-fi genre these days, she's reportedly

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.120
totally down with the idea of a fourth Matrix
film, even if she's not involved in making

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:36.620
it.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.060
In August 2019, she told Slash Film,

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:43.280
"I like it when stories go out into the world
and then come back to you in different ways.

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:45.600
I mean, that's what storytelling is all about.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:46.920
I'm part of a bigger thing.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:51.040
I don't have any ownership over stuff like
that, so whatever story anybody wants to tell,

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.180
I can't wait to hear.

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:54.800
I hope [the fourth Matrix is] better than
the original."

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:58.880
Of course, improving on the original Matrix
is a rather tall order.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:03.720
In fact, one could argue that the first two
sequels didn't exactly rise to the task.

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:07.920
Meanwhile, franchise fatigue is a very real
thing, and it's only getting realer.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:12.680
As you may recall, people were already growing
weary of the Matrix franchise by the time

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.420
The Matrix Revolutions came out.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:17.920
Just look at the dismal reviews for that film
if you don't believe us.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:22.440
But after two long decades away from Neo and
his cohorts, fans might be totally pumped

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:26.640
to plug back into The Matrix…but whether
the fourth film is ultimately a worthwhile

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:28.860
chapter in the saga remains to be seen.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:33.120
The hit-and-miss critical performance of both
the latest Star Wars trilogy and the prequel

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:37.810
trilogy potentially serve as cautionary tales
about what happens when you create new franchise

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:39.220
installments out of thin air.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:43.840
Sure, a studio stands to make billions of
dollars, but time will tell whether these

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:47.920
latter entries ultimately dampen the legacy
of the original trio of films.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:53.220
As for the upcoming Matrix movie, Jonathan
Groff, Neil Patrick Harris and Yahya Abdul-Mateen

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:57.910
II have been cast in super-secretive roles…and
it's rumored that Mateen is playing a younger

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.440
version of Laurence Fishburne's Morpheus character.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:04.840
If that's true, perhaps we should all brace
ourselves for some sort of mind-melting, totally

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:06.620
convoluted time-travel plot.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.440
Meanwhile, a new wave of characters does leave
the door open for more entries down the line.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:12.720
Only time will tell.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:18.200
Back in September 2019, Keanu Reeves weighed
in on the new Matrix screenplay in an interview

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.340
with Entertainment Tonight:

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:20.700
"It's very ambitious.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:22.040
As it should be."

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:27.160
Here's hoping the fourth Matrix doesn't just
trot out the same ideas as its three predecessors.

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:30.860
After all, the world only needs so many sensual
space raves.

